# Q4 — Does serve start with a read-only OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR?
Date: 2026-10-13. All spike containers mount spike/config at /etc/agency:ro
with OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR=/etc/agency. agency-spike-q3 also read-only.

## Commands + trimmed output

$ docker inspect -f '{{.State.Health.Status}}' agency-spike-q3
healthy
$ docker exec agency-spike-q3 touch /etc/agency/probe
touch: cannot touch '/etc/agency/probe': Read-only file system  (rc=1)
$ curl /api/info   (Basic auth, inside container)
{"version":"2.0.26",...}                 # HTTP 200 while config stays ro
$ docker exec agency-spike-q sh -c 'echo CONFIG_DIR=$OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR'
CONFIG_DIR=/etc/agency
$ curl /api/agent/spike | python3 -c '...data.id...'
spike                                # agent from the ro dir loads

## Observation
Yes. Serve boots healthy, serves /api/info, and loads agents/permissions
from a read-only config dir; writes to it fail EROFS while serving is
unaffected (negative case). Hot-reload watches are subscribed (see q12.log
watcher lines); config changes would arrive via remount/recreate, which is
already the fleet's update path (per-expert config rendered at deploy).
Negative case: writing to the read-only config dir fails EROFS (rc=1)
while serve stays healthy and /api/info keeps returning 200.

## Verdict: yes (fallback "bake into image" not needed)
